Z||000002||BC-GT||08-24-2001||10:20 PM||||I think we (the forum) should start hounding Rodney D. about making those. Tough as nails to find in the boneyards.<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||getterw||08-24-2001||10:33 PM||||The Fiero Store (www.fierostore.com) has them for $6 a piece.  Pricey, but new.  Part #60522||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||08-24-2001||11:33 PM||||I bought them from the Fiero Store.  Where they that much?  WOW!  Well, I guess I was just glad to have the.  But go to the junk yard too!  This spring I picked up a set of vents with hardware from a u-pull-it yard for $10 and there is no paint chipping on them.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||flyntus||08-25-2001||03:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by b52buf:<BR><B>Does anyone out there know of a source for the wing type fasteners on the rear compartment grills. I'd like to get the real thing not a substitute.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Here are part numbers & prices from Fiero Store: Part #60522 Deck Lid Vent Screw With Flap $5.95 each.<BR>Part #68301 Rear Louver Vent Screw Washer $2.99 each<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||08-25-2001||03:36 PM||||I just sanded down my vents, and laid a coat of flat black manifold paint. Works great, looks awesome, doesn't peel up with the heat.<BR>As for the pull-tabs, I'd like to put a set on the other panel, just for symetry||||reg||7
Z||000007||Jim Jimenez||08-29-2001||01:30 AM||||The screw, washer and retainer that makes up this part are 20580522, 20358301, and 20375013. They are all still available. <P>Get 'em from your friendly GM parts guy. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||08-29-2001||01:41 AM||||#20358301 is $3.45 (GM list price) or $2.59 wholesale.<P>#20580522 is $5.83 (GM list price) or $4.38 wholesale.<P>I couldn't find a price for #20375013.<P><BR>GMpartsdirect.com is even cheaper ($5.57 for one of each listed), but it's over $20 with shipping! <P>I'd go to your local dealer and order them there......at least you'll save the shipping from the Fiero Store.<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||b52buf||08-29-2001||12:49 PM||||Thanks to all who answered my post.<BR>Your efforts are greatly appreciated. ||||reg||10
